uires the compact-set-to-box and compact-product facts in S001 without declaring or proving them. The M004 hypothesis-check text records compactness but does not prove it or make it a permitted premise. Inputs otherwise have identifiable stated roles.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/applications/1\\\",\\\"/logic/calculations\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"P has the requested integrability, differentiability, and zero-derivative conclusions for every positive r, and the two paragraphs intend to establish them. Since the first compactness step is unsupported, the full output is not derived.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The proof fixes an arbitrary positive r and ends by saying r is arbitrary; the local declarations are scoped to R001 and no temporary assumption or witness is exported. This scope judgment does not validate the unsupported existence/compactness reasoning for B.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/0\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/1\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The M004 application requires B×J compact, but its stated check merely asserts this and S001 provides no proof of compactness of the chosen box product. M001 and M002/M003 application strings also do not independently establish every analytic condition; in any event the earlier compact-domain gap blocks the claimed use of uniform convergence and integration. This is conditional review of the supplied contracts, not source-signature verification.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/applications/1\\\",\\\"/inference/applications/2\\\",\\\"/inference/applications/4\\\",\\\"/inference/applications/5\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The packet states the full cited H/M propositions, P, and the definitions of e, E, and Δx sufficiently to understand the intended output and argument without producer proofs. Some source-contract detail is not independently audited here; that does not supply an additional premise.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/1/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/2/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/3/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/4/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/5/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/6/statement\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/definitions/0\\\",\\\"/definitions/1\\\",\\\"/definitions/2\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The named objects r, J, C_J, and B are declared, but B's witness declaration is based only on H003's compact C_J and does not establish that a closed box containing it exists. The same missing compactness reasoning underlies the claimed compact product. Other symbols are predominantly packet parameters, definitions, or input-bound objects.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/0\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/1\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The factual step from compact C_J to a containing closed box, and the compactness of B×J used for M004, have no direct input or earlier local proof. Therefore actual factual uses in S001 are not closed over the listed inputs and permitted calculations.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks/0\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/3\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The conditional proof is not sufficient from this packet alone because S001's compactness step is unsupported, as detai